 "changes": [
  "World constants: A, B and K come from V7/world_constants.json, made on the cloud's processor (C1). Every gate and v6 check still runs unchanged and exact; a tripwire stops the process if any code computes A or K another way.",
  "Processes at once: up to 16 on the laptop (default 12), instead of version 6's 'at most 2'; none in the cloud after the handoff (C2, C6).",
  "Interrupted phases: a killed phase's files are moved out of v6's output folder (never deleted) and the phase reruns; machine-wide interruptions never count; after phase-specific ones it reruns twice, then once alone, then on the user's --retry, until done (C5). Every other output stays write-once.",
  "Re-made references: on seeds 2-4 only, where the laptop does not reproduce one of the gate's saved reference actors bit for bit (C7's rule), the laptop makes its own copy with the gate's exact call, and only that seed's and world's training phase reads it (stalling-world policy test: 'none' and 'full_none'; no-stall policy test: 'none'; stalling-world full host: 'plain'). Deployment always reads the gate's saved actors.",
  "Check (b) forecast: before anything is approved, the self-test measures whether the laptop's own programs agree as check (b) requires; a gap above 1e-5 makes it NOT READY unless the user chose to proceed (Q7).",
  "Environment: Ubuntu 24.04 in WSL 2, the OpenBLAS kernel left to its default, an exact eight-variable environment per phase, one processor per phase checked in code (C3, C4).",
  "Compute budget: version 6's 'about 72-92 process-hours' stays an estimate that stops nothing; the process-hours actually used are counted and reported (C2).",
  "Records: a ledger of every attempt, provenance files and the probe records (C7, C10, C11)."
 ],
